--- negative control: bg-udp-recv-timeout-not-reported ---
  facility: INET pseudo-device BGn: -- the receive timeout of the executive-resident BGn: driver's IO$_READVBLK (vms_ioctl_bg_recv, src/kernel-core/vms_bg.c, vms-a9e7). A UDP channel (IO$_SETMODE P2=IO$K_SOCK_UDP) armed with TCPIP$C_RCVTIMEO through the IO$_SETMODE P4 socket-option list must complete a read against a silent peer with SS$_TIMEOUT, so the DNS resolver behind $ TELNET/FTP/PING name reports a silent name server instead of hanging.
  defect:   vms_ioctl_bg_recv() maps the host kernel's -EAGAIN (the armed sk_rcvtimeo expiring) to SS$_TIMEOUT. The mutation reports it as SS$_ABORT instead, so the timed-out read still returns promptly (no hang -- the timeout itself is still armed) but with the wrong status: the silent-port read assertion reddens (it requires SS$_TIMEOUT), and so does the resolver's silent-server assertion, because the engine reads SS$_ABORT as a failed exchange (NONET) rather than a timeout. The byte-exact UDP round-trip and every resolver answer path stay green. One conditional expression replaced.
